  "description": "QILBEV crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H102 Er4 Mn2 N4 O34,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.368-3.897 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.41-122.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [MnIII2ErIII4(L1)2(L2)2(μ3-OH)4(μ1,3-pivalate)6(NO3)2]·2CH3CN (C74H108N6O34Mn2Er4; CCDC C70H102Er4Mn2N4O34·2(C2H3N)). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Er(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
